{"time": "2026-06-08T22:34:56", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "a_language_drift_parent_005", "post_id": "obtit69", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "A 'laddered' continuing resolution. Seriously? Two different shutdown deadlines in January and February just to avoid doing the actual job of passing a budget right now. It’s like Congress is trying to invent new ways to procrastinate. Can we please just get some boring, standard governance instead of these endless, over-complicated cliffhangers?"}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:34:56", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "a_language_drift_parent_006", "post_id": "se65n8n", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "It’s exhausting how people expect complex international conflicts to have simple, morally pure solutions. Some situations are just tragic and messy, with no good options. Pretending there's an easy way out doesn't help anyone."}
